    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's interesting. You mentioned that the \"grammatical deviations\" in Witness B's statement might signal a less formalized recollection. \n\nDo you think those linguistic patterns—like the use of double negatives or non-standard verb tense—are actually linked to the accuracy of the memory itself, or is it more about how a jury might subjectively judge their character or education level? I'm trying to help my students understand if they're being biased against the speaker's dialect rather than the facts of the testimony.",
